In article <5501.26eec2be@vax5.cit.cornell.edu> horj@vax5.cit.cornell.edu writes:
>Anyway, my question is this:  among folks out there who have attained this 
>mystical level of "demigod" -- I assume by winning the game by recovering the
>Amulet -- what percentage first did it without "cheating" with saved game
>files; that is, making backups of their better games?  Is it likely to be
>anytime in the near future when I get further than about the 15th level on a
>consistant basis without resorting to this obvious, but underhanded, technique?

I can't vouch for other systems, but being the games administrator of our site,
I can speak for our own.  At our site we've (until very recently) prevented
players from making backups of their save files, and we've still had those
who have managed to make it to demi-god(des) hood.  It is mostly dependent on
a) a good starting character, b) a good knowledge of the game, and c) luck.

Recently, we started up another nethack 'playground' with the permissions set
so that players can make backups, but we do keep the playgrounds separate,
so those who manage great feats without backing up can get recognition apart
from those who just spend many hours getting exactly the right level.

Hope this helps a little!

